{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres","id":1018835,"title":"Which spheres?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-18T10:00:51-08:00","id":1018835,"title":"Which spheres?","content":"Which spheres would I need for the following:<br /> <br /> To command a horde of insects to attack/invade a particular location<br /> <br /> To manipulate nature, such as using vines as tendrils, manipulating wood or trees to attack things, or making roots pop up out of the ground and strangulate someone/manipulating those roots to appear as hands and so on.<br /> <br /> Make grass in a certain area transform into flesh-eating parasites.<br /> <br /> Making plants sprout up and aggressively reclaim an area, and or making plants in an area grow and march towards a certain area<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T10:12:16-08:00","id":1018839,"title":"","content":"#1 Mind 3, possibly Life 2 alone byt thats up to your ST.<br /> <br /> The rest with Life 3<br /> <br /> The quicker you want a reaction / growth and the larger the area you affect will determine the number of successes you will need.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just an afterthought byt if you want the plants to act on their own you will need to give them a mind which will require Mind 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 12-18-2016, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T10:44:24-08:00","id":1018847,"title":"","content":"Or you can awaken the spirit of the plant (Spirit 3), or make possessed plants (Spirit 4) in case you want to circumvent the Mastery of Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T10:44:47-08:00","id":1018848,"title":"","content":"Some may allow you to do a lot of the &quot;make plants to things to people&quot; with Life 2. But you would have to be there making the plants do it, they wouldn't act on their own volition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T11:20:57-08:00","id":1018857,"title":"","content":"Some Prime, or at least Quintessence, can be needed to create matter or volition with just Life 3. With other spheres you can turn those plants ever weirder.<br /> <br /> With Life 3, Forces 3, you can make plants that spit fire or ice, by consuming something. With Prime 3 you can make those plants deal Agg through eating the very Pattern of something. If you have more spheres than Life, you can go wild with ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T12:09:17-08:00","id":1018863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1018857#post1018857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Prime, or at least Quintessence, can be needed to create matter or volition with just Life 3. With other spheres you can turn those plants ever weirder.<br /> <br /> With Life 3, Forces 3, you can make plants that spit fire or ice, by consuming something. With Prime 3 you can make those plants deal Agg through eating the very Pattern of something. If you have more spheres than Life, you can go wild with ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>But to do everything (except the insect commanding) Life 3 would suffice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T13:38:54-08:00","id":1018886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1018863#post1018863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But to do everything (except the insect commanding) Life 3 would suffice?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on what kind of flesh-eating parasite you're talking about.<br /> <br /> Otherwise... yeah.<br /> <br /> Not that, as has been pointed out, there aren't alternative ways of accomplishing the same things by use of other Spheres as well, particularly Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T16:08:42-08:00","id":1018948,"title":"","content":"A single Sphere is always enough to cover its basic concept to its fulles. The power of a Mage is this kind of awesome. If all you want is to transmute living matter into another kind of living matter, so you need nothing else.<br /> <br /> Your ST can require some other things, but it doesn't seems likely in your case. With a secondary sphere at 3 you can turn something that isn't covered by Life into a Life pattern. Matter to make a carnivorous plant out of a statue, Prime to transmute Quintessence into it, seemingly making the plant appear out of nothing, Mind can take the <i>idea</i> of a carnivorous plant into an actual one.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, if you wanted to make things more complex. An intelligent plant need also Mind, one that crumbles stone with a touch needs Matter, one that freezes the air around needs Forces. A point could be made for Matter to create a plant with too much additional mass, or Forces for more energy than the input provided by normal photosynthesis. Those aren't required unless your Paradigm is really too strict or the difference too big, otherwise it is just excessive nitpicking.<br /> <br /> But you didn't went so far. As weird as those plants of yours are, you essentially transmuted a &quot;pure&quot; Life pattern into another &quot;pure&quot; Life pattern. Maybe Mind can help into making the new beings into something well programmed, or actually intelligent, and Correspondence can help you in controlling the result from a distance. But as far as you went, all of this is just Life.<br /> <br /> Do you have a clearer spread of your Spheres for we to help with rotes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T20:16:42-08:00","id":1019025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1018948#post1018948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A single Sphere is always enough to cover its basic concept to its fulles. The power of a Mage is this kind of awesome. If all you want is to transmute living matter into another kind of living matter, so you need nothing else.<br /> <br /> Your ST can require some other things, but it doesn't seems likely in your case. With a secondary sphere at 3 you can turn something that isn't covered by Life into a Life pattern. Matter to make a carnivorous plant out of a statue, Prime to transmute Quintessence into it, seemingly making the plant appear out of nothing, Mind can take the <i>idea</i> of a carnivorous plant into an actual one.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, if you wanted to make things more complex. An intelligent plant need also Mind, one that crumbles stone with a touch needs Matter, one that freezes the air around needs Forces. A point could be made for Matter to create a plant with too much additional mass, or Forces for more energy than the input provided by normal photosynthesis. Those aren't required unless your Paradigm is really too strict or the difference too big, otherwise it is just excessive nitpicking.<br /> <br /> But you didn't went so far. As weird as those plants of yours are, you essentially transmuted a &quot;pure&quot; Life pattern into another &quot;pure&quot; Life pattern. Maybe Mind can help into making the new beings into something well programmed, or actually intelligent, and Correspondence can help you in controlling the result from a distance. But as far as you went, all of this is just Life.<br /> <br /> Do you have a clearer spread of your Spheres for we to help with rotes?</div> </div> </div> </div> How would one use blood magick (influencing other's blood) with life sphere?<br /> <br /> Also, transforming a plant into a man eater and making it attack with my own power (essentially, it's not operating under it's own volition, it's dumb, like a drone) does not require mind, yes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T20:20:34-08:00","id":1019027,"title":"","content":"Also, how do you transform humans, vampires, werewolves, and other supernaturals respectively (with life).<br /> Like, turning them to stone, an animal, a pea, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T20:30:08-08:00","id":1019031,"title":"","content":"To transform other beings, people or supernaturals to another complete form requires Life 5 + the spheres that accompany thier make up. Spirit or Matter 2<br /> <br /> Then you would need matter 2 or 3 to make them a stone or other object.<br /> <br /> Realize this would be at difficuly 9 (vulgar) and need at least 5 successes. Its easier to kill them out right through direct pattern damage ( Life 3 Matter 2 for a vampire) at a much lower difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 12-18-2016, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T21:49:31-08:00","id":1019052,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that be permanently rewriting a Pattern of a sapient creature? Rewriting your own Pattern permanently is a godlike feat (Revised, p. 208), so I imagine it would be just as difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T22:02:06-08:00","id":1019059,"title":"","content":"According to M20 transforming someone into a different shape is 4 successes. <br /> <br /> Changing shape and rewriting a pattern are quite different things. A vampire turned into a rock is still a vampire, hes just shaped like a rock and unable to enguage with the world in most (nearly all) instances. Though the effect may even be made to be permanent it could still be countered.<br /> <br /> If a vampire has his patern rewritten to become a rock the he is nolonger a vampire but a rock and no amount of counter magic will change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T22:59:40-08:00","id":1019083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1019025#post1019025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would one use blood magick (influencing other's blood) with life sphere?<br /> <br /> Also, transforming a plant into a man eater and making it attack with my own power (essentially, it's not operating under it's own volition, it's dumb, like a drone) does not require mind, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood magic depends on what you want to do with said blood. Slowing or speeding up its flow might only require Life 3 (as you're activating natural parts of their physiology, in much the same way you would try to accelerate their natural healing). Ditto Life 3 if you want the blood to attack them from within, since it counts as using Life to harm another creature. Having the blood rip out of their body would need to add Forces 3 + Prime 2, in order to have the proper motive energy to move around how blood normally doesn't. Same if you want to Blood Bend like from Avatar: The Last Airbender, and use their blood to move them around like a grotesque flesh marionette. (Although you could possibly do it with just Forces 3 + Prime 2, if you apply that force to their body generally; Life 4 alone could do the same sort of meat puppet routine, by hijacking the body's muscles for your own purposes). Life 3 would be used to forcibly coagulate the blood in their veins, as could Entropy 4. Changing blood into another substance would require Life 3 + Matter 2 or 3, depending on how the Storyteller feels about it.<br /> <br /> If you have any other sorts of applications of blood control we haven't covered here, ask away. Note finally that most of the above would be Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Turning a plant into a more lethal plant would require life 3, or Life 4 if you're adding features the particular species doesn't have normally (an oak tree with a toothy maw and a digestive tract, for instance). If you're controlling it at the time, it wouldn't require anything else; it is your magical plant puppet. If you wanted it to run on automatic, then it might indeed require Mind, unless you're splicing it with something like a Venus Fly Trap which comes with the inclination to bite down if something enters its mouth.<br /> <br /> I've been promoting a House Rule of mine for a while now, that turns the &quot;Create Mind&quot; business into a graduated feature over the course of Mind 3 to Mind 5. At Mind 3, you can create Expert Systems. Basically, give the &quot;vessel&quot; a set of If/Then statements, allowing it to react in a specific way to specific stimuli. Enough to make a statue move its position, a suit of armor throw an ax down at a particular spot, or have a bush of thorny vines constrict around whoever steps into it. But it can't really do &quot;combat&quot;, since it can't react dynamically to rapidly changing situations.<br /> <br /> Mind 4 gives the being animal level intelligence, with a set of instincts and capacity for emotions, as well as the ability to react from moment to moment. Instead of creating a whomping willow that only hits in an area blindly, it can track an enemy and attack them, such as any tree can. Storyteller fiat as to what senses, if any, a plant has access to. Probably touch or feeling vibrations by default, more if you use Life 4 to give it additional senses like hearing or sight.<br /> <br /> And at Mind 5, you can create True Sapience. Awareness of self, and the ability to think logically, long term. If you want to create a tree that you can hold a conversation with, you need this level. (It's not that animals couldn't talk - some of them can - it's just that their options and understanding are limited; if a dog could talk, their words would be mostly what you'd get anyway by reading their body language and barks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T09:26:02-08:00","id":1019294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1019025#post1019025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, transforming a plant into a man eater and making it attack with my own power (essentially, it's not operating under it's own volition, it's dumb, like a drone) does not require mind, yes?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Note: This answer really has to be Focus specific, particularly with regard to the mage's Sect and their perspective on magic, the Practice and the Instruments of the character involved.<br /> <br /> But, no, not necessarily. Turn the grass into sawgrass and line the edges with fast-acting necrotizing fasciitis bacteria. You don't even need to make the grass move. Enemy walks through it... Comes out the other side with lots of cuts and welts that immediately start to suppurate and rot...<br /> <br /> Please make sure to have a duration on the effect or undo it afterwards. Otherwise, next time a kid and his dog run through the grass, playing.... &lt;shudder&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T15:50:32-08:00","id":1019462,"title":"","content":"Are there any spiritual rotes that denote particular curses I could inflict upon someone as a shaman? If not, what spheres could I use to inflict curses upon someone (like curse them to sickness, to death, to a skin-eating bacteria, to bone deteroriation, etc)<br /> <br /> Also, my char is a Haitian voodooist dreamspeaker. What spheres would I need to be able to do voodoo? Examples being evoking dark forces, using a doll to inflict pain upon someone from afar, etc.<br /> <br /> As for blood magick - to create a ball of boiling blood Id need prime and forces, right? And to create a tendril of it, I'd also need prime and forces?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T19:22:09-08:00","id":1019563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1019025#post1019025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would one use blood magick (influencing other's blood) with life sphere?<br /> <br /> Also, transforming a plant into a man eater and making it attack with my own power (essentially, it's not operating under it's own volition, it's dumb, like a drone) does not require mind, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradigm defines how you do things. Spheres define what you do in the end. They blur a little in the middle, in how action becomes effect, but mostly it surmises this way. So <u>you</u> say <u>me</u> how you use blood magic, first. Do you cut yourself to sympathetically call the blood of your target? Do you draw on the target's blood itself? Do you touch the target to sense blood vessels just across the skin? Once you answer those questions, you'll have the how. The spheres do not depend on it. They depend on <u>what</u> you do with it, to the target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1019027#post1019027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how do you transform humans, vampires, werewolves, and other supernaturals respectively (with life).<br /> Like, turning them to stone, an animal, a pea, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This answer isn't unanimous, because it depends on the ST. Some like to limit what Mages can do to major supernaturals, what is advisable if there are other PCs playing them. If not, Life. Add Mind for Changelings, Matter for Vampires, Spirit for Changers, Wraiths and Demons. The ST can ask for Entropy and/or Prime, depending on personal view and circumstances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1019462#post1019462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any spiritual rotes that denote particular curses I could inflict upon someone as a shaman? If not, what spheres could I use to inflict curses upon someone (like curse them to sickness, to death, to a skin-eating bacteria, to bone deteroriation, etc)<br /> <br /> Also, my char is a Haitian voodooist dreamspeaker. What spheres would I need to be able to do voodoo? Examples being evoking dark forces, using a doll to inflict pain upon someone from afar, etc.<br /> <br /> As for blood magick - to create a ball of boiling blood Id need prime and forces, right? And to create a tendril of it, I'd also need prime and forces?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now we're game!<br /> <br /> You're a Haitian Bokor, that's the <u>how</u>. You do your stuff through voodoo rituals to call the power of the Loa.<br /> <br /> For doing stuff through distances, you'll need Correspondence. Curse is just another way to say Magic. It implies that you'll use it to do bad stuff that stick, but it isn't relevant to define Spheres. What your curse will do? To cause disease of any kind, probably Life and Entropy. To make them destined to die, Entropy. Also for bad luck. A tendril of blood can be done with Forces and Life, the same to boil it. Or with Life and Mind. Or Life alone, to actually turn it into a creature of living blood. Prime is to other things, I won't recommend it for now beyond 2 at most, until you grasp the concept.<br /> <br /> Or you can concentrate on the spirits. You don't need Spirit to do stuff explaining it through spirits, but with Spirit Sphere, you can forego all the math and go right for them. Of course, it does have its own downsides, but maybe will be better for what you want.<br /> <br /> What I suggest to you is to concentrate on the Spirit Sphere and ask actual spirits for stuff. You'll have a lot of leg work with them, but it will probably be more intuitive and versatile. Get Spirit 2, Correspondence 2, and Prime 2 just for the Quint you'll need to bargain with spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T20:45:43-08:00","id":1019592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1019563#post1019563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradigm defines how you do things. Spheres define what you do in the end. They blur a little in the middle, in how action becomes effect, but mostly it surmises this way. So <u>you</u> say <u>me</u> how you use blood magic, first. Do you cut yourself to sympathetically call the blood of your target? Do you draw on the target's blood itself? Do you touch the target to sense blood vessels just across the skin? Once you answer those questions, you'll have the how. The spheres do not depend on it. They depend on <u>what</u> you do with it, to the target.<br /> <br /> <br /> This answer isn't unanimous, because it depends on the ST. Some like to limit what Mages can do to major supernaturals, what is advisable if there are other PCs playing them. If not, Life. Add Mind for Changelings, Matter for Vampires, Spirit for Changers, Wraiths and Demons. The ST can ask for Entropy and/or Prime, depending on personal view and circumstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now we're game!<br /> <br /> You're a Haitian Bokor, that's the <u>how</u>. You do your stuff through voodoo rituals to call the power of the Loa.<br /> <br /> For doing stuff through distances, you'll need Correspondence. Curse is just another way to say Magic. It implies that you'll use it to do bad stuff that stick, but it isn't relevant to define Spheres. What your curse will do? To cause disease of any kind, probably Life and Entropy. To make them destined to die, Entropy. Also for bad luck. A tendril of blood can be done with Forces and Life, the same to boil it. Or with Life and Mind. Or Life alone, to actually turn it into a creature of living blood. Prime is to other things, I won't recommend it for now beyond 2 at most, until you grasp the concept.<br /> <br /> Or you can concentrate on the spirits. You don't need Spirit to do stuff explaining it through spirits, but with Spirit Sphere, you can forego all the math and go right for them. Of course, it does have its own downsides, but maybe will be better for what you want.<br /> <br /> What I suggest to you is to concentrate on the Spirit Sphere and ask actual spirits for stuff. You'll have a lot of leg work with them, but it will probably be more intuitive and versatile. Get Spirit 2, Correspondence 2, and Prime 2 just for the Quint you'll need to bargain with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div> So instead of getting all of these extravagant spheres, I could just stick to a few and in the spirit of a shaman use the spirits for most of my stuff? Use the spirits for combat and defense (fetishes), to do my bidding (summonings) and so on?<br /> <br /> Also, any idea how I'd create a voodoo doll?\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T01:03:43-08:00","id":1019651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1019592#post1019592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So instead of getting all of these extravagant spheres, I could just stick to a few and in the spirit of a shaman use the spirits for most of my stuff? Use the spirits for combat and defense (fetishes), to do my bidding (summonings) and so on?<br /> <br /> Also, any idea how I'd create a voodoo doll?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The upside of Spirit is that, so long as you talk to the right Umbrood, you can get a whole lot of things done with just the one Sphere (though, like monteparnas said, Prime helps when it comes to payment). The downside is that you'll be dependent on those same Umbrood to do anything. You turn into a broker for ephemeral specialists, hiring spiritual contractors to do your work for you. Having other Spheres like Entropy or Life is by no means a bad idea, even if you explain it in Focus as invoking the power of spirits (I know, it's a confusing distinction).<br /> <br /> Plus, working directly with spirits requires a great deal of legwork and resource management. The former because not every spirit above a certain weight class will appreciate being called in by a random shaman. Sometimes to get them to work with you, you have to enter the Umbra and find them. The latter because unlike with using other Spheres to invoke the power of Loa, you can't always sacrifice a couple cigars and a bottle of whiskey to get things done. Working directly with spirits requires a lot of negotiation and haggling.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to say you can't go all Spirit all the time. I'm just saying that it makes the game more complicated, both for you and for your Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Voodoo Doll is, at its core, just another Instrument. Which Spheres it requires depends on what you want done, although unless you are using said doll in the target's presence, you will require Correspondence no matter what. Harming (or healing) the target requires Life, assaulting them with the elements will require Forces, giving them bad luck requires Entropy, etc. Once you've made the doll in the likeness of your target (requiring a Craft roll), you'll need something to tie the doll to the person. Hair, blood, nail clippings, other body samples, or a personal possession. If you know the target well personally, you might be able to skip that step, because YOU act as a sufficiently close tie. Once you've got the doll, do what thou wilt with whatever Sphere is needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:36:59-08:00","id":1019788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1018835-which-spheres?p=1019592#post1019592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So instead of getting all of these extravagant spheres, I could just stick to a few and in the spirit of a shaman use the spirits for most of my stuff? Use the spirits for combat and defense (fetishes), to do my bidding (summonings) and so on?<br /> <br /> Also, any idea how I'd create a voodoo doll?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Bluecho said it all, but I'll try to be simpler. Also, I think that just Spirit will be better for you, given your difficulty for now grasping the more nuanced concepts of the game.<br /> <br /> You can. It isn't ideal, but you can, and for now I think you should.<br /> <br /> Other Spheres will serve for you to do stuff yourself. You can explain stuff in the game by invoking the Loa without using Spirit, and then do things yourself.<br /> <br /> Using Spirit alone, all your magic will actually affect are spirits. You'll be dependent on them, they can be messed with by rivals, they can be hard to deal with sometimes, as I said before, it will be a lot of legwork, because you'll do nothing by yourself, only through spiritual entities. But it works, in the end of the day, and should work mostly in the way you would think your magic as a shaman works.<br /> <br /> A Voodoo doll is just the How, so you can do it whatever you want. For this system, it is mostly description. What a Voodoo doll does, though, is something you'll need Correspondence for, mostly Correspondence 2. The doll is just a Focus/Instrument, that is, the descriptive factor of your effect. Don't worry too much about it, but get Correspondence 2.<br /> <br /> Since you have to haggle with Spirits, Prime 2 will be a must to have Quintessence at hand. For spirits, it is the energy they use. You'll descriptively do a lot of things for them, because of their metaphysical nature. Sometimes you'll have to do little, just be thankful. But sometimes they can get stingier prices. Then you ease things with some Quint.<br /> <br /> With this strategy, you'll be fine as long as you remember that spirits are characters by their own, they're full-fledged-if-weird NPCs.<br /> <br /> If you want to do things by your own, then Spheres cover the final effect. Life seems what you'll want more, by the things you ask, Entropy's a second. In that case, you still describe things by your shamanism, maybe offering cigars and stuff to the Loa of the blood, but your own magic is doing things. It simplifies some things. You still need Correspondence for the Voodoo doll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}